<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- The bound vendor tool carries no entitlement either, for the same reason
     one step further down: its parent (arkforged) is not sandboxed, so an
     inherited sandbox has nothing to inherit from.

     This is byte-identical in intent to ArkDeck's own TASK-BRC-003 contract for
     the App-bundled component (ArkDeckApp/RockchipComponent.entitlements). The
     shipped ArkDeck.app component was measured on 2026-08-16 and carries an
     empty dictionary in both the XML and DER entitlement slots.

     USB reaches the tool because neither process is sandboxed, not because a
     capability was granted. If an in-process USB backend ever lands here, this
     file stops being obviously correct — see the review trigger in
     docs/decisions/AFD-0003-arkforged-signing-packaging.md. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
